# OMJEP Design Quality Rules

Use these references only as inspiration:
- .cursor/references/design/shadcn-ui
- .cursor/references/design/magicui
- .cursor/references/design/shadcnspace
- .cursor/references/design/shadcn-dashboard-template

Do not copy full files blindly.
Do not replace the app architecture.
Do not add heavy dependencies unless explicitly approved.

## OMJEP visual direction

OMJEP is not a generic SaaS dashboard.
It is an esports platform with:
- FIFA / FUT inspired player cards
- premium gaming dashboards
- club identity
- mercato economy
- competitions and schedules

## Design style

Dark mode:
- navy / slate background, never pure black
- elevated cards
- subtle glow
- readable text

Light mode:
- soft slate background
- white elevated cards
- clear borders
- no pale low-contrast text

Colors:
- Mauve = primary action
- Cobalt = league / sport data
- Gold = premium / UCL / legendary
- Green = success
- Red = errors only

## Components quality

Every UI change must include:
- empty state
- loading state
- error state
- mobile behavior
- light/dark readability

## Forbidden

Never modify:
- backend
- DB
- auth
- proxy
- deploy
- global theme
unless explicitly requested.

Never add:
- random gradients everywhere
- unreadable glassmorphism
- text-black on dark
- text-white on light
- giant animations that hurt performance

## Before coding

For visual work, first describe:
1. visual goal
2. exact pages
3. components to touch
4. references used
5. expected QA checklist
